{"name":"Sun Dance","hex":"#c4aa4d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sun dance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of sundance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun_dance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sun Dance","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun Dance is a ceremony practiced by some Native Americans in the United States and Indigenous peoples in Canada, primarily those of the Plains cultures, as well as a new movement within Native American religions. Members of otherwise independent bands gather to reaffirm beliefs about the world and the supernatural through rituals of personal and community sacrifice. Typically, young men would dance semi-continuously for several days and nights without eating or drinking; in some cultures, self-mortification was or is currently also practiced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_Dance"},{"title":"Sun Dance (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sun Dance is the first part of the fifth studio album Sun Dance & Penny Rain released by Aimer. It was released on April 10, 2019 in a regular CD only edition and with Penny Rain in three versions: a limited 2 CD + 2 BD + Special Storage Box + Sun Dance Jigsaw Puzzle, a limited 2 CD + BD edition (Type-A), and a limited 2CD + DVD edition (Type-B). Sun Dance and Penny Rain were Aimer's first new studio albums since daydream in 2016. In addition, Sun Dance is Aimer's first album to be solely produced by agehasprings since her 2012 debut album Sleepless Nights."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/40/Aimer_Sun_Dance.jpg/330px-Aimer_Sun_Dance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_Dance_(album)"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Fort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sun dance, Shoshone at Fort Hall, 1925","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFort_Hall_Reservation._Shoshone_Indian_Sun_Dance_-_NARA_-_298649.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Wind_River_Shoshone_Sun_Dance_lodge.png/500px-Wind_River_Shoshone_Sun_Dance_lodge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Wind_River_Shoshone_Sun_Dance_lodge.png/1280px-Wind_River_Shoshone_Sun_Dance_lodge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Wind_River_Shoshone_Sun_Dance_lodge.png/500px-Wind_River_Shoshone_Sun_Dance_lodge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diagram of an Eastern Shoshone Sun Dance lodge.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWind_River_Shoshone_Sun_Dance_lodge.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Annual_report_of_the_Bureau_of_Ethnology_to_the_Secretary_of_the_Smithsonian_Institution_%281889%29_%2814774538232%29.jpg/500px-Annual_report_of_the_Bureau_of_Ethnology_to_the_Secretary_of_the_Smithsonian_Institution_%281889%29_%2814774538232%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Annual_report_of_the_Bureau_of_Ethnology_to_the_Secretary_of_the_Smithsonian_Institution_%281889%29_%2814774538232%29.jpg/1280px-Annual_report_of_the_Bureau_of_Ethnology_to_the_Secretary_of_the_Smithsonian_Instituti